    "proximate_text": "The direct cause of the pressure control valve oscillations was a loose threaded connection for the LVRT driver plate on the hydraulic actuator for Main Turbine Control Valve 1 N11 F026D. ... Vibration on equipment was determined to cause equipment issues with alignment, assembly fasteners to loosen, and assembly parts critical to the function of the actuator assembly to back out.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "inadequate engineering evaluation of vibration effects on turbine control valve actuator; less than adequate vendor oversight",
    "provisional": true
  },
