  "notes": "Two distinct scram events reported together: (1) manual scram due to Main Turbine HP Control Valve actuator/LVRT connection issue with two stated root causes (engineering evaluation of vibration effects; vendor oversight), and (2) subsequent automatic scram ~32 minutes later due to unrelated Feedwater Startup Level Control Valve malfunction (volume booster replaced). Cause code left TBD/provisional per FORM-366 despite narrative providing detailed root causes, per rule 4 (official code governs; narrative gave no coded cause). No previous similar events per licensee statement, so no SIMILAR_TO edge or stub LER emitted. RPS modeled as System with null eiis_code since no bracket code given in text for RPS itself (only TA and SJ codes were bracketed)."
